   "reason": "Rewind restores the enemy side to the start of their last turn, which brings back an ally they just ate — so the single-charge Dragon can be replayed after a mistake instead of ending the run, and at T3+ the rewind also stuns the king. | Boulder needs no movement and King form needs no safety, so Rookie can stand in the middle of the guard set, immune, and spend turns bricking the pen shut — the only real cost is the move limit.",
